  "summary": "BPFDoor is a passive Linux backdoor used for long-term persistence, attributed to Red Menshen. It uses a Berkeley Packet Filter (BPF) to stealthily monitor network traffic for a magic packet, which activates a reverse or bind shell. The malware employs various anti-forensic techniques, such as process name spoofing and placing itself in temporary filesystems like /dev/shm.",
